Introduction
============
The PIILUS package includes the implementation of the Parallel Improved Incomplete LU with Skyline Storage preconditioning technique 
in C++ programming language. The package also includes an implementation of the Implicit Preconditioned Bi-Conjugate Gradient Stabilized
iterative method based on the PIILUS scheme. Functions for reading and writing Matrix Market files are also provided.


Installation
============
Building the PIILUS software is performed by the issuing the following command on the root folder:
   make

Before issuing ``make'' command in the terminal, the full Intel environment (Intel oneAPI) should be (initially installed and then) 
sourced, i.e: source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh.

External Libraries
==================
This PIILUS package requires the following external libraries:

Intel oneAPI - This library contains optimized verions of BLAS, LAPACK and other software packages and is required by IPBiCGSTAB. The
	            library can be downloaded from https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/oneapi/onemkl-download.html for
               different operating systems.


Example Programs
================
The directory example/ includes an example file on how to use the PIILUS package to solve large unsymmetric sparse linear systems.
The number of threads for parallel execution is controlled by the environmental variable `OMP_NUM_THREADS=nthreads`.
